    A011["<div class='arg'><b>A011 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The hawkish presser sees 30Y rates lower by 5-10bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside growth risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to downside inflation risk.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are lower due to a more credible Fed return to orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh continues to sound inflation impatient.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh suggests recent data does not imply an adequate disinflation trend.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The market raises the hike peak.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A012["<div class='arg'><b>A012 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The hawkish hike supports the author's constructive long end asset swap spread view.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower growth risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower inflation risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Enhanced Fed credibility supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A013["<div class='arg'><b>A013 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The dovish presser sees 30Y rates higher by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are higher due to dovish Fed action.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond yields are higher due to confusion about Warsh policy direction or reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Warsh implies few hikes to follow.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>IM:</b> The dovish presser sees 2Y rates lower by 5bps.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A014["<div class='arg'><b>A014 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>There is a sharp twist steepening of the curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Twist steepening comes from a lower near term policy path.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Twist steepening comes from a perceived very high bar to hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Twist steepening comes from long end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Long end rates reflect a higher inflation risk premium.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Long end rates reflect a Warsh credibility discount.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed surprisingly holds.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>IM:</b> Over time, the 30Y increases towards 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A015["<div class='arg'><b>A015 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed hold represents an unprecedented dovish hold (using FOMC OIS data back to '07).</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed does not hike.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A016["<div class='arg'><b>A016 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
