    A018["<div class='arg'><b>A018 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD is supported.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed hikes at least 100bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed brings current expectations forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>RI:</b> Chair Warsh's aversion to forward guidance makes the bullish USD case challenging.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The SEP shows broadening support for additional hikes (relative to the June SEP).</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Inflation forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Chair Warsh himself, intentionally or unintentionally, offers some indication that a more prolonged campaign is necessary to return inflation on the path to 2%.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A019["<div class='arg'><b>A019 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD softens with dovish or non-committal language from Warsh.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Markets do not have the patience for anything that sounds like a #quot;one and done#quot; type event under the veil of #quot;no forward guidance#quot;.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The USD falls in tandem with rising back-end yields.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
